Deal seven lanes: two verifications owed on repairs, five repair groups\n\nVF60 takes FIX163's two families -- FIX163 repaired both and rendered no pixels,\nso verification is owed to a lane that is neither FIX163 nor VF54 and must\nre-derive the pixels rather than carry VF54's forward.\n\nVF61 takes il-seal-3yr-set and mn_petition_15218-set, each repaired byte-free by\na lane that cannot certify its own repair.\n\nFIX167 groups nj_ordinance-set, oh_marijuana_expungement-set and\nri_nonconviction_sealing-set into one lane because all three share the\nbuild-census-v1-nj_arrest_no_conviction-set.mjs host; splitting them would put\nthree lanes in one builder.\n\nFIX168, FIX169, FIX170 and FIX171 take eight families whose FAIL verdicts have\nstood unrepaired. Four of them (sd_arrest_expungement-set, ar-felony-seal-set,\nin_infraction_nondisclosure-set, fl-early-juvenile-set) fail SOURCE_IDENTITY at\nbases that predate the shared-record pin refresh, so each lane must re-derive\nthe finding at current HEAD before repairing anything.\n\nEvery grant is a transfer from the lane that recorded it, not a fresh assert:\na released grant reverts to its originally-recorded lane, and choosing a\nreleased grant's destination is a dispatch act.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01W3FAJNotS5DdvyJS1khjid","timestamp":"2026-09-10T18:14:38Z","author":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"},"committer":{"name":"Claude","email":"noreply@anthropic.com"}},"repository":{"id":1248656766,"node_id":"R_kgDOSmz9fg","name":"legalease-partner-dashboard-clean","full_name":"Roger-LegalEase/legalease-partner-dashboard-clean","private":false,"owner":{"login":"Roger-LegalEase","id":287531360,"node_id":"U_kgDOESNhYA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/287531360?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Roger-LegalEase","html_url":"https://github.com/Roger-LegalEase","followers_url":"https://